  "text": "So why risk paying people at all? Because airlines are balancing two costs. Cost one: a seat leaves empty and can never be sold again. Cost two: too many people show up and the airline pays to fix the problem. The goal is not, \"sell as many tickets as possible.\" It's: sell just enough extra tickets that the expected empty-seat loss is smaller than the expected overbooking cost.",
